      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This really needs to be implemented. Either this or a proper chat system for desktop and mobile players. \n\nI play with a friend who struggles with audio processing (and I do as well, along with being situationally mute), so we both use the chat feature relatively often.\n\nHowever, due to being unable to read the chat history, we often have to repeat ourselves, get timed out for spam, and then while we're waiting for the timeout to end, the chat bugs and doesn't display the text properly.\n\nAdditionally, something not mentioned here—the utter lack of privacy. People are able to see the words as they're typed (which imo defeats the purpose of \"sending\" the message). It's also awkward for me personally as I'm dyslexic, and my friend and I are both autistic and often script/rephrase things several times, so it's a very out there of us both messing up what we're trying to say, retyping, and everyone seeing us doing it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
